        + "Nothing is kept unless you tick it; only counts are recorded.";

    static final String MESSAGES_SAYS =
        "Reads, in the one message-backup file you choose, the conversations and messages \u2014 only when you pick it and tap Look, only on the phone. "
        + "Nothing is kept unless you tick it; only counts are recorded.";

    static final String SENDERS_SAYS =
        "Lets you say that a sender of service messages is not about your obligations. Orb remembers only your answer, against a key that reveals nothing, "
        + "and uses it to leave those messages out of what it reads from a message backup you choose. Nothing leaves the phone. You can take any answer back.";

    static final String OBS_KEEP_SAYS =
        "Keeps the facts Orb reads from a source you choose \u2014 an amount, a day, which service and what kind of fact \u2014 sealed on this phone, one bundle for each "
        + "source and month, for 24 months, so that your money ledger and your obligations survive after you delete the backup file. It never keeps a message or "
        + "any of its words. Nothing leaves the phone. Switching it off stops keeping and erases nothing; erasing what was kept is a separate choice you make.";

    static final String CALLS_SAYS =
        "Reads your call history \u2014 the number, time, length and kind of each call in the last year \u2014 only while a person's page is open, only on the phone, "
        + "to say when you last spoke. Nothing is kept; only how many calls were looked at is recorded.";

    static final String UNDERSTAND_SAYS =
        "Draws together what you have already allowed Orb to see \u2014 your contacts, your calls and the things you kept \u2014 into plain things it has noticed, "
        + "such as who you are in regular touch with; only while the People screen is open, only on the phone. It uses a source only if that source is on. "
        + "Nothing is kept except your answer to each one; nothing leaves the phone.";

    static final String BRIEF_SAYS =
        "Shows one notification each morning, at a time you chose, with counts of what is overdue and ahead \u2014 counts only, unless you ask for the first words. "
        + "It uses only what Orb already holds; nothing leaves the phone. On the lock screen it says only that your morning brief is ready. "
        + "You can turn it off at any time.";

    /** The declarations, in the order the screen shows them. */
    static final List<Declaration> ALL = Collections.unmodifiableList(Arrays.asList(
        new Declaration(PACKAGES, 1L, "Which apps are installed", PACKAGES_SAYS, TIER_OBSERVE,
            "your grant — a recorded decision", Arrays.asList("grants.packages"),
            "Package scanning: revoke", true,
            Arrays.asList("GrantReader", "PackageQueries", "DeclaredPackages", "Watch", "PackageAccess")),
        new Declaration(SCREEN, 1L, "The text of a screen, when you ask", SCREEN_SAYS, TIER_OBSERVE,
            "your allow-list, one app at a time, and your invoking it every time",
            Arrays.asList("orb.assist.captured", "orb.assist.declined"),
            "Apps Orb may remember from: remove", true,
            Arrays.asList("ScreenReader", "AssistSession", "UpiApps")),
        new Declaration(GRANTS, 1L, "Which apps hold powerful settings", GRANTS_SAYS, TIER_OBSERVE,
            "always on — it needs no permission and protects you", Arrays.asList("grants.observed"),
            "not switchable", false,
            Arrays.asList("GrantReader", "Grants", "Watch")),
        new Declaration(CONTACTS, 1L, "Who your contacts are, when you open People", CONTACTS_SAYS, TIER_OBSERVE,
            "your grant — a recorded decision — and Android's own permission",
            Arrays.asList(ContactsFacts.READ), "Revoke contacts access", true,
            Arrays.asList("ContactsReader", "ContactsAccess", "PeopleActivity")),
        new Declaration(APPSEC, APPSEC_VERSION, "What the apps on your phone may do", APPSEC_SAYS, TIER_OBSERVE,
            "your grant \u2014 a recorded decision \u2014 and your running the check", Arrays.asList(SafetyFacts.CHECKED),
            "Revoke the safety check", true,
            Arrays.asList("AppSecurityReader", "SafetyAccess", "SafetyActivity")),
        new Declaration(DOCUMENTS, DOCUMENTS_VERSION, "PDFs in a folder you chose", DOCUMENTS_SAYS, TIER_OBSERVE,
            "your grant \u2014 a recorded decision \u2014 the folder you chose, and your tapping Look now", Arrays.asList(DocumentsFacts.LOOKED),
            "Switch off the Documents source", true,
            Arrays.asList("DocumentsReader", "DocumentsAccess", "SourcesActivity")),
        new Declaration(MESSAGES, MESSAGES_VERSION, "Text messages from a backup file you choose", MESSAGES_SAYS, TIER_OBSERVE,
            "your grant \u2014 a recorded decision \u2014 the file you pick, and your tapping Look", Arrays.asList(MessagesFacts.LOOKED_TYPE),
            "Switch off the Messages source", true,
            Arrays.asList("MessagesReader", "MessagesAccess", "SourcesActivity")),
        new Declaration(SENDERS, SENDERS_VERSION, "Senders that are not about your obligations", SENDERS_SAYS, TIER_OBSERVE,
            "your grant \u2014 a recorded decision, made at your first mark \u2014 and your own answer for each sender", Arrays.asList(SenderFacts.JUDGED),
            "Switch off sender marks", true,
            Arrays.asList("SenderRules", "SenderFacts", "SendersAccess", "Senders", "SenderSession", "SendersActivity")),
        new Declaration(OBS_KEEP, OBS_KEEP_VERSION, "The facts Orb has read, kept sealed", OBS_KEEP_SAYS, TIER_OBSERVE,
            "your grant \u2014 a recorded decision, made when you first say yes to keeping \u2014 and your tapping Keep each time", Arrays.asList(ObservationFacts.KEPT),
            "Switch off keeping facts", true,
            Arrays.asList("ObservationStore", "ObservationFacts", "KeepAccess", "Ledger", "LedgerActivity", "SourcesActivity")),
        new Declaration(CALLS, CALLS_VERSION, "When you last spoke with someone", CALLS_SAYS, TIER_OBSERVE,
            "your grant \u2014 a recorded decision \u2014 Android's own permission, and a person's page being open (only in the calls build)", Arrays.asList(CallsFacts.READ),
            "Switch off the call-history line", true,
            Arrays.asList("CallsReader", "CallsAccess", "PeopleActivity")),
        new Declaration(UNDERSTAND, UNDERSTAND_VERSION, "What Orb has noticed about your people", UNDERSTAND_SAYS, TIER_OBSERVE,
            "your grant \u2014 a recorded decision \u2014 and your own answer to each thing it suggests", Arrays.asList(UnderstandingFacts.READ),
            "Switch off What Orb has noticed", true,
            Arrays.asList("UnderstandingAccess", "UnderstandingRules", "UnderstandingFacts", "Understanding")),
        new Declaration(BRIEF, BRIEF_VERSION, "A morning brief", BRIEF_SAYS, TIER_ACT_REVERSIBLE,
            "your grant \u2014 a recorded decision, standing because a morning brief exists to appear when you are not looking \u2014 and the gate at each showing", Arrays.asList(BriefFacts.SHOWN),
            "Switch off the morning brief", true,
            Arrays.asList("BriefRules", "BriefFacts", "BriefConfig", "Brief", "BriefAlarms", "BriefNotifier", "BriefReceiver")),
        new Declaration(Reminders.CAPABILITY, Reminders.VERSION, "A reminder you set", Reminders.DECLARATION, TIER_ACT_REVERSIBLE,
            "your confirmation of each reminder", Arrays.asList("orb.action.released"),
            "What Orb may do: turn off", true,
            Collections.<String>emptyList()),
        new Declaration(Handoff.CAPABILITY, Handoff.VERSION, "Reach a person from their page", Handoff.DECLARATION, TIER_ACT_REVERSIBLE,
            "your confirmation of each hand-off, every time", Arrays.asList(HandoffFacts.RELEASED),
            "What Orb may do: turn off", true,
            Arrays.asList("Handoff", "HandoffFacts", "HandoffFlow"))));

    static Declaration byId(String id) {
        for (Declaration d : ALL) if (d.id.equals(id)) return d;
        return null;
    }

    /** What the platform APIs are, by name, that Orb's reads are made with — each allowed only in the files a declaration names. */
    static final List<String> READ_APIS = Collections.unmodifiableList(Arrays.asList(
        "getInstalledPackages", "getInstalledApplications", "queryIntentActivities", "queryBroadcastReceivers", "queryIntentServices",
        "getActiveAdmins", "Settings.Secure", "enabled_notification_listeners", "AssistStructure", "ViewNode",
        "onHandleScreenshot", "takeScreenshot", "ContactsContract", "READ_CONTACTS",
        "getInstallSourceInfo", "requestedPermissions", "isDeviceSecure", "ADB_ENABLED", "ENABLED_INPUT_METHODS",
        "DocumentsContract", "PdfRenderer", "getTextContents", "OPEN_DOCUMENT_TREE",
        "CallLog"));

    /** Reads Orb does not have. They appear nowhere in the source until a capability declares them. */
    static final List<String> UNDECLARED_READS = Collections.unmodifiableList(Arrays.asList(
        "CalendarContract", "LocationManager", "FusedLocation", "UsageStatsManager", "AudioRecord", "MediaRecorder",
        "CameraManager", "ClipboardManager", "getPrimaryClip", "TelephonyManager", "SmsManager", "READ_SMS",
        "BODY_SENSORS", "Telephony.Sms", "content://sms", "ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION", "READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE", "READ_MEDIA_IMAGES"));

    // ---- state and last use: projections over the journal, never stored

    /** What the journal says about one capability right now. */
    static final class Status {
        /** `ON`, `OFF` or `ALWAYS ON`, with the count that matters, in words. */
        final String state;
        /** When it was last used, in epoch ms, or -1 if never. */
        final long lastAtMs;
        /** What the last use came to — counts only, never content. */
        final String lastDetail;

        Status(String state, long lastAtMs, String lastDetail) {
            this.state = state;
            this.lastAtMs = lastAtMs;
            this.lastDetail = lastDetail;
        }
    }

    private static final Pattern WALL_CLOCK = Pattern.compile("\"wallClock\":(\\d+)");

    private static String lastOfType(List<String> lines, String type) {
        String found = null;
        for (String line : lines) if (type.equals(Journal.typeOf(line))) found = line;
        return found;
    }

    /** The last event of a type that also carries `"source":"<source>"` in its payload — the documents and messages sources share their event types. */
    private static String lastOfTypeFrom(List<String> lines, String type, String source) {
        String found = null;
        for (String line : lines) if (type.equals(Journal.typeOf(line)) && line.contains("\"source\":\"" + source + "\"")) found = line;
        return found;
    }

    private static long wallClock(String line) {
        if (line == null) return -1L;
        Matcher m = WALL_CLOCK.matcher(line);
        return m.find() ? Long.parseLong(m.group(1)) : -1L;
    }

    private static long number(String line, String key) {
        if (line == null) return -1L;
        int payload = line.indexOf("\"payload\":");
        Matcher m = Pattern.compile("\"" + Pattern.quote(key) + "\":(\\d+)").matcher(line);
        return payload >= 0 && m.find(payload) ? Long.parseLong(m.group(1)) : -1L;
    }

    private static String word(String line, String key) {
        if (line == null) return "";
        int payload = line.indexOf("\"payload\":");
        Matcher m = Pattern.compile("\"" + Pattern.quote(key) + "\":\"([A-Za-z]+)\"").matcher(line);
        return payload >= 0 && m.find(payload) ? m.group(1) : "";
    }

    private static boolean flagFalse(String line, String key) {
        return line != null && line.contains("\"" + key + "\":false");
    }

    static Status status(String id, List<String> lines) {
        if (PACKAGES.equals(id)) {
            boolean granted;
            try {
                granted = PackageGrants.lastIsGrant(lines);
            } catch (java.io.IOException unreadable) {
                // A line whose type cannot be read: the history cannot say, so neither does this.
                return new Status("unknown — the history could not be read", -1L, "");
            }
            String scan = lastOfType(lines, "grants.packages");
            long count = number(scan, "installedPackageHoldingCount");
            String detail = scan == null ? "never"
                : flagFalse(scan, "installedPackageReadable") ? "could not read (not granted)"
                : count >= 0 ? count + " apps" : "read";
            return new Status(granted ? "ON — you granted it" : "OFF — not granted", wallClock(scan), detail);
        }
        if (SCREEN.equals(id)) {
            int apps = AllowList.allowed(lines).size();
            String captured = lastOfType(lines, "orb.assist.captured");
            return new Status(apps == 0 ? "OFF — no app is allowed" : "ON — " + apps + (apps == 1 ? " app allowed" : " apps allowed"),
                wallClock(captured), captured == null ? "nothing remembered yet" : "something was remembered");
        }
        if (CONTACTS.equals(id)) {
            boolean granted;
            try {
                granted = PackageGrants.lastIsGrant(lines, CONTACTS);
            } catch (java.io.IOException unreadable) {
                return new Status("unknown — the history could not be read", -1L, "");
            }
            String read = lastOfType(lines, ContactsFacts.READ);
            long contacts = number(read, "contacts");
            long people = number(read, "people");
            long possible = Math.max(0L, number(read, "possible"));
            String detail = read == null ? "never" : contacts + (contacts == 1 ? " contact" : " contacts") + " looked at, " + people + (people == 1 ? " person" : " people")
                + " tied by number or email, " + possible + " only by a name";
            return new Status(granted ? "ON — you granted it" : "OFF — not granted", wallClock(read), detail);
        }
        if (Handoff.CAPABILITY.equals(id)) {
            int opened = 0;
            for (String line : lines) if (HandoffFacts.RELEASED.equals(Journal.typeOf(line))) opened++;
            String released = lastOfType(lines, HandoffFacts.RELEASED);
            String state = Handoff.enabled(lines) ? "ON — every tap is confirmed" : "OFF — you turned it off";
            return new Status(state, wallClock(released), released == null ? "none opened yet" : opened + " opened — Orb sent nothing");
        }
        if (APPSEC.equals(id)) {
            boolean granted;
            try {
                granted = PackageGrants.lastIsGrant(lines, APPSEC);
            } catch (java.io.IOException unreadable) {
                return new Status("unknown \u2014 the history could not be read", -1L, "");
            }
            String checked = lastOfType(lines, SafetyFacts.CHECKED);
            long apps = number(checked, "apps");
            long now = number(checked, "now");
            long review = number(checked, "review");
            String detail = checked == null ? "never run" : apps + " apps looked at, " + now + " to look at now, " + review + " worth a look";
            return new Status(granted ? "ON \u2014 you granted it" : "OFF \u2014 not granted", wallClock(checked), detail);
        }
        if (CALLS.equals(id)) {
            boolean granted;
            try {
                granted = PackageGrants.lastIsGrant(lines, CALLS);
            } catch (java.io.IOException unreadable) {
                return new Status("unknown \u2014 the history could not be read", -1L, "");
            }
            String read = lastOfType(lines, CallsFacts.READ);
            String detail = read == null ? "never looked" : number(read, "examined") + " calls examined, " + number(read, "matched") + " with that person, at the last look";
            return new Status(granted ? "ON \u2014 you granted it" : "OFF \u2014 not granted", wallClock(read), detail);
        }
        if (BRIEF.equals(id)) {
            boolean granted;
            try {
                granted = PackageGrants.lastIsGrant(lines, BRIEF);
            } catch (java.io.IOException unreadable) {
                return new Status("unknown \u2014 the history could not be read", -1L, "");
            }
            String shown = lastOfType(lines, BriefFacts.SHOWN);
            String skipped = lastOfType(lines, BriefFacts.SKIPPED);
            boolean lastWasShown = shown != null && wallClock(shown) >= wallClock(skipped);
            String detail;
            if (shown == null && skipped == null) detail = "never shown";
            else if (lastWasShown) detail = "last shown: " + number(shown, "overdue") + " overdue, " + number(shown, "today") + " due today, " + number(shown, "waiting") + " waiting for, "
                + number(shown, "dates") + " dates this week";
            else detail = "last not shown: " + word(skipped, "reason");
            return new Status(granted ? "ON \u2014 at " + BriefRules.clock(BriefConfig.minute(lines)) : "OFF \u2014 not turned on", Math.max(wallClock(shown), wallClock(skipped)), detail);
        }
        if (UNDERSTAND.equals(id)) {
            boolean granted;
            try {
                granted = PackageGrants.lastIsGrant(lines, UNDERSTAND);
            } catch (java.io.IOException unreadable) {
                return new Status("unknown \u2014 the history could not be read", -1L, "");
            }
            String read = lastOfType(lines, UnderstandingFacts.READ);
            String detail = read == null ? "never opened" : number(read, "asked") + " to confirm, " + number(read, "confirmed") + " you said yes to, "
                + number(read, "rejected") + " you said no to, at the last look";
            return new Status(granted ? "ON \u2014 you granted it" : "OFF \u2014 not granted", wallClock(read), detail);
        }
        if (MESSAGES.equals(id)) {
            boolean granted;
            try {
                granted = PackageGrants.lastIsGrant(lines, MESSAGES);
            } catch (java.io.IOException unreadable) {
                return new Status("unknown \u2014 the history could not be read", -1L, "");
            }
            String looked = lastOfTypeFrom(lines, MessagesFacts.LOOKED_TYPE, MessagesFacts.SOURCE);
            long kept = 0L;
            for (String line : lines) if (MessagesFacts.KEPT_TYPE.equals(Journal.typeOf(line)) && line.contains("\"source\":\"" + MessagesFacts.SOURCE + "\"")) kept += Math.max(0L, number(line, "kept"));
            String detail = looked == null ? "never looked" : number(looked, "conversations") + " conversations in the last file, " + kept + " months kept in all";
            return new Status(granted ? "ON \u2014 you granted it" : "OFF \u2014 not granted", wallClock(looked), detail);
        }
        if (SENDERS.equals(id)) {
            boolean granted;
            try {
                granted = PackageGrants.lastIsGrant(lines, SENDERS);
            } catch (java.io.IOException unreadable) {
                return new Status("unknown \u2014 the history could not be read", -1L, "");
            }
            String last = lastOfType(lines, SenderFacts.JUDGED);
            int quiet = SenderFacts.quietCount(lines);
            return new Status(granted ? "ON \u2014 you granted it" : "OFF \u2014 not granted", wallClock(last), last == null ? "no sender marked" : quiet + (quiet == 1 ? " sender is" : " senders are") + " quiet");
        }
        if (OBS_KEEP.equals(id)) {
            boolean granted;
            try {
                granted = PackageGrants.lastIsGrant(lines, OBS_KEEP);
            } catch (java.io.IOException unreadable) {
                return new Status("unknown \u2014 the history could not be read", -1L, "");
            }
            String last = lastOfType(lines, ObservationFacts.KEPT);
            int bundles = ObservationStore.bundles(lines);
            return new Status(granted ? "ON \u2014 you granted it" : "OFF \u2014 not granted", wallClock(last), last == null ? "nothing kept yet" : bundles + (bundles == 1 ? " bundle" : " bundles") + " kept");
        }
        if (DOCUMENTS.equals(id)) {
            boolean granted;
            try {
                granted = PackageGrants.lastIsGrant(lines, DOCUMENTS);
            } catch (java.io.IOException unreadable) {
                return new Status("unknown \u2014 the history could not be read", -1L, "");
            }
            String looked = lastOfTypeFrom(lines, DocumentsFacts.LOOKED, DocumentsFacts.SOURCE);
            long kept = 0L;
            for (String line : lines) if (DocumentsFacts.KEPT.equals(Journal.typeOf(line)) && line.contains("\"source\":\"" + DocumentsFacts.SOURCE + "\"")) kept += Math.max(0L, number(line, "kept"));
            String detail = looked == null ? "never looked" : number(looked, "found") + " PDFs found at the last look, " + kept + " kept in all";
            return new Status(granted ? "ON \u2014 you granted it" : "OFF \u2014 not granted", wallClock(looked), detail);
        }
        if (GRANTS.equals(id)) {
            String observed = lastOfType(lines, "grants.observed");
            return new Status("ALWAYS ON", wallClock(observed), observed == null ? "never" : "looked");
        }
        if (Reminders.CAPABILITY.equals(id)) {
            int waiting = Reminders.pending(lines).size();
            String released = lastOfType(lines, ActionFacts.RELEASED);
            String state = Reminders.enabled(lines) ? "ON — " + waiting + (waiting == 1 ? " reminder waiting" : " reminders waiting") : "OFF — you turned it off";
            return new Status(state, wallClock(released), released == null ? "none shown yet" : "shown");
        }
        return new Status("unknown", -1L, "");
    }

    /** The declared ids, for tests and the screen. */
    static List<String> ids() {
        List<String> out = new ArrayList<>();
        for (Declaration d : ALL) out.add(d.id);
        return out;
    }
}
